# Implementação do Semantic Release

Utilizar Semantic Release como mecanismo oficial de versionamento.

A implementação deve seguir as boas práticas da documentação oficial.

Utilizar preferencialmente:

- semantic-release
- @semantic-release/git
- @semantic-release/github
- @semantic-release/changelog
- @semantic-release/commit-analyzer
- @semantic-release/release-notes-generator

Gerar automaticamente:

- Git Tag
- GitHub Release
- CHANGELOG.md

---

# Exemplo de Workflow - Alpha

```yaml
name: Alpha Release

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - "release/*"

permissions:
  contents: write
  pull-requests: write

jobs:
  alpha:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0

      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 20

      - run: npm ci

      - run: npx semantic-release
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
```

---

# Exemplo de Workflow - Beta

O Workflow deverá ser executado quando o Pull Request possuir a Label:

```
beta
```

Exemplo:

```yaml
on:
  pull_request:
    types:
      - labeled
```

Validar:

```
github.event.label.name == 'beta'
```

Caso verdadeiro

executar

```
semantic-release
```

utilizando o canal

```
beta
```

---

# Exemplo de Workflow - Release Final

Executar quando

```
Pull Request

↓

Merged

↓

main
```

Exemplo

```yaml
on:
  pull_request:
    branches:
      - main
    types:
      - closed
```

Validar

```
merged == true
```

Executar

```
semantic-release
```

Gerando

```
1.2.0
```

